INT. SALT WAREHOUSE - DAWN

Mountains of grey salt. Rafters. Dust in slanted light.

SERGEANT ODALYS BRANTZ, 40s, cracked lips, rifle slung low, drags a wounded boy through the doorway.

PVT. TEODOR "TEDDY" VASKO, 19, bleeding thigh, grips her collar.

CORPORAL HIROSHI MAEDA, 30s, wire-thin, covers the door. Counts rounds. Counts again.

BRANTZ
Down. Behind the big pile.

VASKO
I can walk.

BRANTZ
You can't.

MAEDA
(muttering)
Eleven. Eleven. Eleven.

Boots outside. Gravel. Stop.

Brantz and Maeda freeze. Vasko stops breathing.

BRANTZ
(whisper, to Maeda)
Window.

MAEDA
Boarded.

VASKO
Sarge, I hear--

BRANTZ
Quiet.

MAEDA
Sarge, they're at the--

VASKO
They're at the back too.

BRANTZ
Everyone shut up.

A shadow crosses the slats. Gone.

MAEDA
(to himself)
Breathe. Count. Breathe.

Brantz slides a canteen to Vasko. He fumbles it. It clangs.

All three flinch.

A shout outside. Another. Running feet.

BRANTZ
(to all)
Positions. Now.

Vasko drags himself behind a salt drift. Maeda drops to one knee. Brantz climbs a crate.

MAEDA
How many?

BRANTZ
Enough.

VASKO
Sarge, I can't feel my leg.

BRANTZ
Then you can't feel it hurt. Good.

The door shudders. A rifle butt splinters the wood.

Maeda fires. Brantz fires. Salt sprays like snow.

VASKO
I got one! I got--

MAEDA
Down, Teddy!

BRANTZ
Maeda, left!

The door bursts. A grenade skitters across the floor.

All three scatter. Brantz dives for Vasko. Maeda hurls himself at the grenade, kicks it back out the door.

BOOM. Salt rains from the rafters.

Silence. Ringing ears.

MAEDA
(coughing)
Eleven. Ten.

Brantz hauls Vasko up. Vasko grins, white with salt.

VASKO
Still here.

BRANTZ
Move.
